### G4 evaluator timeout hardening re-run

`evaluator/run.mjs` now gives every `./run` command a 20-second timeout, launches each child in its own process group, and kills that group on timeout (SIGTERM with SIGKILL escalation). Timeout failures report `command timed out: <argv>`. Before terminating the command, the evaluator sets the service fixture's hold state to false, releasing any held response; fixture teardown also terminates outstanding command groups and the fixture/sidecar group. A 200-second global watchdog emits a JSON result with each not-yet-evaluated requirement false and error `evaluator watchdog`, then exits nonzero.

