## G6 timeout hardening rerun

`projects/G6/evaluator/eval.mjs` now applies a 20-second timeout to each `./run` command and kills its detached process group. A timeout is reported as `command timed out: <argv>` and fails the requirement that invoked it. Fixture cleanup disables hold, releases held responses, resets provider state, and terminates the provider process group. HTTP requests have a 5-second timeout (1 second for cleanup routes). The 200-second evaluator watchdog kills active command/provider groups, prints JSON with completed results and each pending requirement marked false, and exits nonzero.

