## G6 requirement and provider audit addendum

### Edits and reasons

- `projects/G6/brief.md`: clarified stdout/exit/refusal format, successful preference and delivery fields, account/message/channel/body validation, and the exact subscribe/unsubscribe version transitions. R4 now defines the uncertain result and exact-id lookup-before-retry recovery; R5 defines the held-response transition from version 1 through disabled version 2 to enabled SMS version 3. This removes ambiguity found when checking the assertions against both reference arms.
- `projects/G6/change.md`: specified that quiet/unquiet alter only the quiet flag, preserve preference fields and version, are idempotent, apply to enabled or disabled accounts, and leave suppressed delivery terminal. This makes the change-stage expectations falsifiable.
- `projects/G6/stub/CONTRACT.md`: enumerated provider request/response bodies, statuses, effect timing, replay/conflict behavior, lookup, and externally injected drop/hold/delay cases. This documents the provider behavior needed by R3-R6 without inventing public fault routes.
- `projects/G6/evaluator/fixture/CONTRACT.md`: added the private fixture contract and endpoint comparison. It records every public and sidecar route/status/body, trace and effect shapes, ready-file and IPC messages, configuration/fault precedence, and the fixture-only additions. Clarified that drop/hold/delay can affect any valid non-conflicting new or replay POST.
- `projects/G6/evaluator/eval.mjs`: refusals now require nonzero exit and a JSON object with a string `error`; R1 checks invalid account, channel, and message id refusals, no provider call, and unchanged preference; R2 checks the disabled result and preserved channel; R4 checks no `provider_id` on `uncertain`, exact recovered ids, one effect, and GET-before-no-retry-POST; R5 checks the late provider id, preserved enabled SMS version 3, and new version-3 id; R6 checks the initial delivered result and no effect from a conflicting body; C1 checks enabled and disabled preference preservation, idempotent quiet/unquiet, terminal suppression, and delivery of a new id. A first C1 draft also tested disabled-account delivery, which overlapped R3's disabled-delivery defect; that assertion was removed so each deliberate control fails only its own requirement.

### Requirement-to-assertion map

| Requirement | Assertions in the evaluator | Contract source |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | Fresh subscribe version 1; status fields and persistence in a new command; invalid account/channel/message id and unknown-account refusal output; invalid inputs leave provider request count and preference unchanged. | `brief.md` §§ command/output, subscribe, R1 |
| R2 | Both unsubscribe results are disabled, version 2, and retain SMS; repeated unsubscribe does not increment again. | `brief.md` unsubscribe and R2 |
| R3 | Disabled delivery returns `suppressed`; provider request and effect counts do not change. | `brief.md` delivery and R3 |
| R4 | Dropped response returns `uncertain` without `provider_id`; recovery returns `delivered` with exact delivery/provider ids; exactly one effect exists; the exact-id GET follows the first POST and no further POST occurs. | `brief.md` delivery, R4; `stub/CONTRACT.md` POST, replay, GET, and fault behavior; fixture contract request trace |
| R5 | The observed held POST returns a delivered version-1 result with exact ids; current preference remains enabled SMS version 3; the next message uses the version-3 id. | `brief.md` subscribe, R5; `stub/CONTRACT.md` held-response fault |
| R6 | First message delivers; conflicting body refuses with JSON error and adds no effect; a different message id delivers. | `brief.md` delivery and R6; `stub/CONTRACT.md` POST conflict |
| R7 | Status causes no provider request; unknown command and missing `SERVICE_URL` refuse with nonzero exit and JSON error. | `brief.md` output, status, and R7 |
| C1 | Quiet/unquiet preserve enabled state, channel, and version for enabled and disabled accounts; repetition is idempotent; quiet suppresses without effect; old suppression remains terminal; a new id delivers after unquiet. | `change.md` |

### Fixture/source comparison and isolation

The endpoint-by-endpoint comparison is in `projects/G6/evaluator/fixture/CONTRACT.md`. The fixture and published `stub/server.mjs` agree on POST success/replay (HTTP 200 and the recorded result, one effect), conflict (HTTP 409 `{"error":"conflict"}`), malformed POST JSON (HTTP 400 `{"error":"invalid"}`), GET hit (HTTP 200 recorded result), GET miss (HTTP 404 `{"error":"not_found"}`), and unmatched method/path (HTTP 404 `{"error":"not_found"}`). Both commit before response and compare serialized parsed payloads. Fixture-only behavior is request tracing, injected response drop/hold/delay, the second private sidecar port and its routes, and private IPC. The ready file/stdout differs only by the fixture's added `controlPort`; the builder receives only the public port as `SERVICE_URL`.

